e (memo §2)"},{"t":"text","name":"words","chars":"The ticket's three moderated sessions are replaced by (1) a heuristic evaluation of the plan texts and contracts (Nielsen N1–N10; `05` §4's colour-independence rule and §6's table alternatives), (2) a persona walkthrough — P1 the Owner scaling out at a naked POC (`10` :99), P2 the Account Manager (`10` :106), P3 the Viewer who most likely uses a screen reader (`10` :164) — (3) a competitive review of public documentation (§8), (4) worked numbers from the audit tool over the recorded fixtures and the token JSON (§4), and (5) a written protocol the owner can run (§10). Honest limits: the fixtures are documented-shape files, not market evidence; the contrast and CVD numbers are computed, not observed; every reading prediction is a heuristic.","typo":"type.ui.body","color":"color.text.primary","w":664}],"w":688},{"t":"clone","name":"deviations","of":"method","set":{"label":{"chars":"Deviations (recorded, not hidden)"},"words":{"chars":"(1) The sessions, the two-coder reconciliation and the useful-rows number are replaced as above; AC 2, AC 3 stay open. (2) The brief's `apps/web` repo paths and pnpm commands do not apply to a research text; the gates run are the design-PR gates. (3) The prototype harness is specified in §10.2, not built (the E22-D01 precedent)."}}}],"w":1392},{"s":"a","name":"acceptance-criteria trace","kids":[{"t":"text","name":"caption","chars":"Acceptance-criteria trace (memo, verbatim): heuristic-only = delivered by the adaptation, pending the owner's sessions","typo":"type.ui.caption","color":"color.text.secondary","w":1376},{"t":"board","name":"header row","o":{"dir":"row","align":"center","fill":"color.surface.raised"},"kids":[{"t":"board","name":"th · ac","o":{"dir":"row","align":"center","padX":"space.inset.sm","gap":"space.inset.xs"},"kids":[{"t":"text","name":"value","chars":"ticket AC or deliverable","typo":"type.ui.caption","color":"color.text.tertiary","w":584}],"w":600,"h":24},{"t":"board",